Yeah, the only reason Nethack 'hjkl' direction control felt comfortable
when I first started playing was because of my previous experience with
Vim.  In light of that, the very first thing I should have said is:

1. Move the cursor as you'd move your @ in Nethack.  (except only hjkl,
no diagonal)
2. After placing the cursor where you want to edit, press 'i' to
'i'nsert text as you wish.
3. Press 'esc' to go back into "cursor navigation" mode.
4. When finished editing, press ':wq' to 'w'rite changes and 'q'uit.

There, how's that for a barebones intro to Vi(m) use!

Sidenote:
Does anyone here actually use the numerical pad for navigation?  I
